00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,280
Mr. Hui,

2
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,590
please stop.

3
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:10,480
Don't think we won't shoot you.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:14,830
Fire then.

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,070
Once I'm dead,

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,440
you'll be completely free of trouble.

7
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,090
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

8
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,290
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

9
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,200
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

10
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,630
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

11
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:18,610
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

12
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:22,770
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

13
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:27,560
♪I'm willing to wait♪

14
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:31,250
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

15
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:34,050
♪I want to share my life with you♪

16
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:40,470
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

17
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:42,620
♪In this cold and gray city♪

18
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,330
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

19
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:46,780
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

20
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:47,440
♪Stay with me♪

21
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:50,190
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

22
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:50,970
♪Stay with me♪

23
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:53,890
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

24
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:56,390
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

25
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:59,430
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

26
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,470
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

27
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:06,690
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

28
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:10,100
[Ash]
[Episode 1]

29
00:03:05,470 --> 00:03:07,310
Great shot.

30
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,430
Let's see who's stronger.

31
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:10,870
I'm stronger.

32
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,630
Mr. Wong.

33
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:18,680
Hey, don't just stand here.

34
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:20,000
Go greet him.

35
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,080
What? Not interested in any of them?

36
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:28,280
I can ask the manager to change them if you want.

37
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,680
Feel free to ask me for whatever you want.

38
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,030
Mr. Wong,

39
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,120
I'm here to discuss business.

40
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:36,360
Or have you changed your mind?

41
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:37,630
Loek To,

42
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,680
don't put it that way.

43
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:42,190
Everyone in Hong Kong, China, knows no one dares cross you.

44
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,500
[Land Acquisition Proposal]

45
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:53,310
This contract contains the terms we agreed on before.

46
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:58,000
I'll give you the land at the original price plus five percent.

47
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:02,030
After that, Tin Ping Group will handle everything.

48
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,800
Sign here.

49
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,150
Loek To,

50
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:11,710
don't say I'm not giving you a fair deal.

51
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:13,710
We're all in business

52
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:15,000
to make money.

53
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:17,510
You say you'll give me five percent more,

54
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,120
but Feros offered

55
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:21,750
twenty percent more.

56
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,270
They even said they have a new project they want to do with me.

57
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,630
You know how you'd choose.

58
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,950
Feros

59
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:34,040
has only been in Hong Kong, China, for less than a year.

60
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,720
They haven't even released their financial results.

61
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,950
Aren't you worried they're making you a promise they can't keep?

62
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,120
Let's not talk about this.

63
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,160
I don't want to ruin our relationship.

64
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:48,630
If you don't like playing snooker,

65
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:50,600
why don't we go somewhere else?

66
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,430
What?

67
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,390
What do you mean?

68
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:13,510
Mr. Wong, I remember you used to be a Mr. Cheung.

69
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:16,680
You married into the Wong family

70
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,870
and even changed your surname.

71
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,240
I thought you were deeply devoted to Mrs. Wong.

72
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,600
Turns out you only did it to climb the ladder.

73
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,430
You see,

74
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,000
my wife isn't a naive woman.

75
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:35,190
You don't think she'll care if I fool around with other women, do you?

76
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,390
Of course I know Mrs. Wong is very generous.

77
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,430
She doesn't mind you fooling around outside.

78
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,830
But what if she finds out about this?

79
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:57,510
Is it really okay, Mr. Wong?

80
00:05:59,070 --> 00:05:59,830
Tell me.

81
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:01,870
What exactly do you want?

82
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:05,680
I told you. I'm here to discuss business.

83
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:07,630
Whether we can reach a deal

84
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,240
is up to you.

85
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:23,540
[Parking Lot Entrance/Exit]

86
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,680
Things went pretty smoothly, right?

87
00:06:25,430 --> 00:06:26,600
He's got plenty of dirt on him,

88
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:28,000
and he still has the nerve to pull tricks.

89
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,630
There's a charity auction tonight.

90
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,160
Not going.

91
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:33,830
What?

92
00:06:34,630 --> 00:06:35,830
I said I'm not going.

93
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,830
Who's the assistant here,

94
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,040
you or me?

95
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,600
Either I take you home,

96
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:45,830
or we call it a day right here.

97
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,000
So cocky, huh?

98
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,270
Fung!

99
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,510
Run, Boss!

100
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:17,750
Don't run!

101
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:26,870
I saved the last pineapple bun

102
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:27,920
for you.

103
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:28,680
Thanks, sir.

104
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,190
I'll finish it and leave.

105
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,510
Take your time.

106
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:38,390
Get back!

107
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:39,920
Don't go!

108
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,680
Knife attack!

109
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,950
[Sluggish]

110
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:54,950
What happened?

111
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,260
[May Business Prosper]

112
00:08:22,430 --> 00:08:23,190
Get up.

113
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,310
This has nothing to do with me.

114
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,000
If you're not involved, get out of here.

115
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,840
I don't care about what's going on between you.

116
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:39,200
You ruined my pineapple bun.

117
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,510
How are you going to make it up to me?

118
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:41,910
Enough nonsense.

119
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:43,670
Trying to play the hero, huh?

120
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:59,150
♪Meeting you feels electric. Is it dangerous?♪

121
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:03,240
♪One look sets the whole room on fire♪

122
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:07,600
♪I see secrets flickering in your eyes♪

123
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:11,500
♪Half a second face-to-face, my heart skips a beat♪

124
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,560
♪The dark night tempts my heart♪

125
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:18,130
♪Breath and heartbeat race out of control♪

126
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:22,180
♪Can't wait. I'm going all in♪

127
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:26,580
♪I declare war and break this deadlock♪

128
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:33,030
♪Who takes the bait? Who can walk away?♪

129
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:37,520
♪Prey and hunter lock eyes. Who has the edge?♪

130
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:41,930
♪One pulls back, one moves in, the heat slowly rises♪

131
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:22,390
Thanks.

132
00:10:23,670 --> 00:10:25,870
I just dealt with a bunch of thugs for a CEO of a listed company.

133
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,910
All I get is a "thanks"?

134
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,200
Do you know who I am?

135
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:31,670
CEO of Tin Ping Group,

136
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:32,840
Hui Loek To.

137
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:35,960
The famous bachelor of the business world.

138
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,030
If I didn't know you,

139
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,720
how could I tell people I run with the big boys?

140
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,320
No one will find this place.

141
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:41,080
Sit wherever you like.

142
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,120
Hey, where is this?

143
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,600
Come on.

144
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:00,750
I'll clean your wounds.

145
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,200
No need.

146
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:04,720
Take off your vest.

147
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:10,720
You hurt your back, didn't you?

148
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,600
I said I'm fine.

149
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Come on.

150
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,200
Slowly.

151
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,510
That's quite a bad injury.

152
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,550
Does it hurt?

153
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,390
Do you know what you're doing?

154
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,910
You're afraid of pain, snowflake?

155
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,600
I'm just teasing you.

156
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:04,550
Easy, okay?

157
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,200
There you go.

158
00:12:24,390 --> 00:12:25,150
That's it?

159
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,550
What else do you want?

160
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:29,720
This isn't a hospital.

161
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,720
Come on. My turn.

162
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,030
Seriously?

163
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:07,630
Darn it.

164
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:10,550
You're just as afraid of pain.

165
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,840
Hurry up.

166
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:34,910
There you go.

167
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,600
Didn't expect the CEO to be so thoughtful.

168
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,270
Got a cigarette?

169
00:13:55,670 --> 00:13:56,390
Thanks.

170
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:11,750
Give me one.

171
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:16,840
You hurt your waist, not your hand.

172
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:18,960
I'm hurt all over.

173
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Do you want to check everywhere one by one?

174
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:06,510
Did it burn you?

175
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:07,840
Yeah.

176
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:08,720
You punk.

177
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:13,970
♪Like we're in love on the edge of a cliff♪

178
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:18,010
♪How thrilling can it really be?♪

179
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:24,340
♪I only win your love by fooling myself♪

180
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,680
♪Love beneath a crumbling wall♪

181
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:32,090
♪Brings far too much heartache♪

182
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,780
♪I hate that I should♪

183
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,440
♪Walk away♪

184
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,440
My car is here.

185
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:10,270
I never owe anyone

186
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,480
a favor.

187
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,200
How can I contact you?

188
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:17,630
Cheung Wai Keung.

189
00:16:25,870 --> 00:16:28,480
This was my first time meeting Hui Loek To.

190
00:16:29,750 --> 00:16:31,910
Back then, I never imagined

191
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,910
anything would happen between us.

192
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:45,150
[Six months later]

193
00:16:50,670 --> 00:16:52,670
[I miss you. Meet you at home.]

194
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,200
Yee Gor.

195
00:17:21,830 --> 00:17:22,790
How's the progress?

196
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:24,440
We're rushing the work.

197
00:17:24,590 --> 00:17:25,640
I've called everyone in.

198
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,830
They haven't slept for several days.

199
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,110
We'll definitely

200
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:28,960
get it done for you.

201
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:30,640
Did anyone get sticky fingers?

202
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:33,440
No.

203
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:34,440
No?

204
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,200
Good.

205
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,880
Just kidding.

206
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,590
Tell them if they do a good job

207
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,400
this time,

208
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:46,110
there'll be more work coming.

209
00:17:46,510 --> 00:17:47,680
Got it.

210
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:21,030
[When can we meet?]

211
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,510
Mr. Hui,

212
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:38,160
you're only half an hour late today. Punctual.

213
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:39,960
Let's begin.

214
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,400
The development plan for Bay Area Metropolis

215
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,440
has been revised.

216
00:18:46,790 --> 00:18:48,270
All the materials are here.

217
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:52,000
I've been following this project

218
00:18:52,030 --> 00:18:53,160
from the start.

219
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:56,110
All the figures are within reasonable and controllable limits.

220
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:57,960
What's there to change?

221
00:18:58,510 --> 00:18:59,510
Just move forward with it.

222
00:19:01,030 --> 00:19:01,790
Here.

223
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:04,830
I think we can lower the relocation compensation

224
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,070
by another ten percent.

225
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:09,400
That'll help us cut costs further

226
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:11,400
and increase the group's profits.

227
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:12,880
Why not?

228
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:16,070
All you ever talk about is increasing profits.

229
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:18,350
You never consider the risks behind it.

230
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:20,920
The current compensation standards

231
00:19:21,070 --> 00:19:23,200
are based on the assessment

232
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,350
by Tin Ping Group's professional team.

233
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,830
If we cut it by another ten percent,

234
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,030
it'll lead to a strike

235
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:30,030
and delay the project.

236
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:32,920
The losses then will be far more than ten percent.

237
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:36,240
This is Tin Ping's flagship project.

238
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:38,400
We can't cut costs at every turn.

239
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:40,880
If the residents protest,

240
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:43,110
we'll naturally have ways to deal with them.

241
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:45,510
Do we really need to care about a few ordinary citizens?

242
00:19:46,070 --> 00:19:47,350
Bringing in the gangs again?

243
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:49,960
Are you getting Sheng Tung involved

244
00:19:50,030 --> 00:19:50,920
to clear them out overnight

245
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,440
and drive them out before they have time to react?

246
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:55,720
You really think the gangs are untouchable?

247
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,640
Hey, anyone inside?

248
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:04,160
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

249
00:20:04,830 --> 00:20:05,720
Let me in and take a look.

250
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,480
Are you insane?

251
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:12,750
What else can we do?

252
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,680
Hey, anyone inside?

253
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,400
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

254
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,240
Anyone inside?

255
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,030
Coming. Wait a second.

256
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:32,830
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

257
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,110
Let me take a look.

258
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,720
Coming.

259
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:38,590
What's wrong?

260
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,400
Hello, sir.

261
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:40,680
The unit downstairs is complaining about water dripping from your place.

262
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:41,750
What are you guys doing?

263
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:43,790
I'm so sorry.

264
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,200
I was doing some renovation and burst a water pipe.

265
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,880
I'm taking care of it now.

266
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:49,920
Can you let me in for a look?

267
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,790
I need to report back.

268
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,030
There's nothing to see.

269
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,030
Can't you see I'm soaking wet?

270
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,640
What? Want to take a shower with me?

271
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:57,640
I'll fix it right away.

272
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:59,310
You really have to fix it right away.

273
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,440
Otherwise, we'll get another complaint.

274
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,270
It'll be a hassle.

275
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,030
Alright.

276
00:21:02,070 --> 00:21:03,160
No problem.

277
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,200
Such a pain.

278
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:16,790
It's done, Yee Gor.

279
00:21:20,270 --> 00:21:21,590
Pretentious.

280
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,270
K.

281
00:21:25,510 --> 00:21:26,750
Are you sick in the head?

282
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:29,030
You've been in this for years.

283
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,440
Your mouth always gets ahead of your brain.

284
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:32,480
How can you be this stupid?

285
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,240
Sorry, Yee Gor.

286
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:38,350
Listen up, everyone.

287
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,510
In two nights,

288
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,830
we'll be making a deal with Lee Fu.

289
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,480
Stay sharp.

290
00:21:46,070 --> 00:21:46,790
Don't screw this up.

291
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,310
Got it?

292
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,440
- Got it, Yee Gor. - Got it, Yee Gor.

293
00:21:53,070 --> 00:21:54,270
It's not that the gangs are all-powerful.

294
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,070
They can act without regard for the rules.

295
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:00,960
To deal with this kind of thing, you need to be ruthless

296
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,200
and nip it in the bud.

297
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,350
When your dad was still alive,

298
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:07,240
it was that ruthlessness that kept the Hui family standing.

299
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,680
That's how Sheng Tung and Tin Ping

300
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,790
grew to the size they are today.

301
00:22:13,590 --> 00:22:14,790
If you keep

302
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:16,160
worrying about every little thing

303
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,240
and hesitating like this,

304
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:19,960
Tin Ping would've been finished.

305
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:21,640
Nip it in the bud?

306
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:23,720
What era are we living in?

307
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:26,030
Anyone can upload a video to the Internet on a whim.

308
00:22:26,070 --> 00:22:27,200
Then it won't just be the project that's in trouble.

309
00:22:27,270 --> 00:22:29,160
You'll be bringing trouble down on yourself too.

310
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,640
Can you bear the consequences?

311
00:22:32,510 --> 00:22:33,270
Loek To.

312
00:22:35,070 --> 00:22:35,680
Fine.

313
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:37,920
Who do you think is right?

314
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,440
Me or Vincent?

315
00:22:41,270 --> 00:22:42,240
Mrs. Hui,

316
00:22:42,270 --> 00:22:43,240
you've thought this through carefully.

317
00:22:43,270 --> 00:22:46,000
Lowering the compensation can indeed increase profits.

318
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,030
I've said it many times.

319
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,880
For the Bay Area Metropolis project,

320
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,440
we'll proceed with the plan exactly as I said.

321
00:22:52,270 --> 00:22:53,680
Anyone who still objects

322
00:22:53,750 --> 00:22:54,440
can get out.

323
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:55,790
Yes, Vincent is right.

324
00:22:55,830 --> 00:22:57,030
We'll proceed with your plan.

325
00:22:57,070 --> 00:22:59,030
Then we'll go with Vincent's plan.

326
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,480
Since there's nothing to discuss,

327
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,830
we'll do it your way.

328
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:06,590
If anything goes wrong,

329
00:23:06,830 --> 00:23:08,240
you'll be responsible.

330
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,880
I'm the CEO.

331
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,590
If anything happens, I'll take responsibility.

332
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:15,720
Have it on my desk by eight tomorrow morning.

333
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,240
If anything goes wrong, I'll hold you accountable.

334
00:23:17,830 --> 00:23:18,750
Understood. I'll get it done.

335
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:20,640
Meeting adjourned.

336
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,480
What else is it?

337
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,200
Your uncle came to see me recently.

338
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,750
He said business hasn't been going well lately.

339
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:38,680
He wants to find some work at Sheng Tung's casino.

340
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:42,640
I was wondering if you could help him get his foot in the door.

341
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,400
What do you think?

342
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:46,640
I don't agree.

343
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:49,680
Third Uncle is a terrible person.

344
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:50,640
He's greedy.

345
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:51,920
Worst of all, he's a gambler.

346
00:23:52,510 --> 00:23:54,680
If we let him join Sheng Tung, it'll only cause trouble sooner or later.

347
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:56,160
And I'll have to clean up the mess again.

348
00:23:57,070 --> 00:23:58,200
I know what you're thinking.

349
00:23:58,790 --> 00:24:00,510
But he's our family.

350
00:24:01,030 --> 00:24:02,550
You have to do this.

351
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,440
If you won't arrange it,

352
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:07,030
I'll have Luk King handle it.

353
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:10,240
Your Third Uncle is very fond of him too.

354
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:12,030
They get along quite well.

355
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,200
No.

356
00:24:13,790 --> 00:24:15,110
I've told you before,

357
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:17,480
Luk King can't get involved in Sheng Tung's business.

358
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:19,030
He's too honest.

359
00:24:19,070 --> 00:24:20,400
How could he stand up to Third Uncle?

360
00:24:20,590 --> 00:24:22,350
If something goes wrong, what if he gets dragged into it too?

361
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,440
I did promise you.

362
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,110
So what?

363
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:26,000
You're a Hui.

364
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:27,790
You have to take responsibility for your own family.

365
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,640
If you won't even help your own uncle,

366
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,400
how will you earn everyone's respect?

367
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:34,960
If your dad had handled things the way you do...

368
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:37,110
Stop bringing up Dad every chance you get.

369
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:39,030
If his way had worked,

370
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:41,720
he wouldn't have left me with such a huge mess after he died.

371
00:24:41,830 --> 00:24:43,160
If he was right,

372
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:45,030
he'd be sitting here today, not me.

373
00:24:45,070 --> 00:24:46,960
Then I wouldn't have to go to his grave every year.

374
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,270
Do whatever you want.

375
00:24:51,790 --> 00:24:52,640
I have nothing more to say.

376
00:25:18,070 --> 00:25:19,480
What's on the schedule next?

377
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:22,200
We're about to leave for the land auction.

378
00:25:26,070 --> 00:25:26,830
Go on.

379
00:25:27,510 --> 00:25:30,920
After that, there's a business reception at the convention center tonight

380
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:34,270
for a Middle Eastern prince opening a family office in Hong Kong, China.

381
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:37,590
Your schedule is packed for the rest of the week.

382
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:40,160
Do you want me to leave some time for yourself?

383
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:45,400
No.

384
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:47,790
Let's take care of the important things first.

385
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:48,960
Okay.

386
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,070
Listen up, everyone.

387
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:03,240
In two nights,

388
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:06,550
we'll be making a deal with Lee Fu.

389
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,200
Stay sharp.

390
00:26:08,790 --> 00:26:09,510
Don't screw this up.

391
00:26:10,590 --> 00:26:11,030
Two days.

392
00:26:12,830 --> 00:26:13,960
Two days.

393
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:23,110
You could've come even later.

394
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:24,680
I'm fine with it. No problem.

395
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,160
Take it off.

396
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,480
Huh?

397
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:44,960
Didn't you say you needed to see me urgently?

398
00:26:45,830 --> 00:26:47,000
Don't waste my time.

399
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:51,480
Go away.

400
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,310
I won't say it twice.

401
00:27:07,830 --> 00:27:09,750
If you don't want me touching you,

402
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,110
then don't ask me to come.

403
00:27:45,310 --> 00:27:47,000
I told you not to move.

404
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:57,720
Had enough?

405
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,510
Who's in a hurry now?

406
00:28:21,030 --> 00:28:22,640
Stop moving around.

407
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:35,160
You're pretty bossy, Mr. Hui.

408
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:38,240
If you wanted me to tie you up,

409
00:28:38,830 --> 00:28:40,030
you could've just said so.

410
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,590
Take this off.

411
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,790
You asked for this.

412
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:52,750
How else am I supposed to take my clothes off?

413
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,590
You don't have to.

414
00:31:57,640 --> 00:31:59,240
Want a beer?

415
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,640
Is beer all you've got?

416
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:11,070
What else would Young Master Hui like?

417
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:15,790
Smoked whiskey, made with applewood, oak, and all that...

418
00:32:15,830 --> 00:32:17,030
I don't know anything about smoked whiskey.

419
00:32:17,070 --> 00:32:18,310
It's just a gimmick.

420
00:32:32,590 --> 00:32:33,350
Smoked beer.

421
00:32:34,070 --> 00:32:35,110
You can only get it here.

422
00:32:42,750 --> 00:32:43,720
Cheers.

423
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:52,880
If you want whiskey,

424
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:54,640
I know a pretty famous bar.

425
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:57,110
We can go together sometime.

426
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:59,030
Are you asking me out?

427
00:33:00,790 --> 00:33:01,510
Fine.

428
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,200
Forget I said anything.

429
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:05,960
Don't dodge my question.

430
00:33:07,070 --> 00:33:08,350
Our relationship

431
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:10,200
only exists between that door and this bed.

432
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,790
Once you walk out, you're nothing to me.

433
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:15,400
It's just a beer.

434
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:17,030
Do you have to make it sound so serious?

435
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:20,200
I can't let people know I'm seeing a thug.

436
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:21,550
Do you understand?

437
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,030
Am I embarrassing you now?

438
00:33:27,830 --> 00:33:28,720
Yes.

439
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,640
Next time, think it through first

440
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:34,070
before asking me something.

441
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:37,110
Next time?

442
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:40,400
Next time, do it yourself.

443
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:42,030
What is wrong with you?

444
00:33:45,790 --> 00:33:48,110
The space between the door and the bed

445
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,160
isn't our space.

446
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:50,440
It's your own space.

447
00:33:50,510 --> 00:33:52,790
I can walk out anytime I want.

448
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:53,790
But you?

449
00:33:53,830 --> 00:33:55,000
Once you walk out that door,

450
00:33:55,030 --> 00:33:56,720
you won't even have the guts to face yourself.

451
00:33:56,790 --> 00:33:58,030
Say that again.

452
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:00,480
I'll say it. What can you do about it?

453
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:04,590
You don't even have the guts to go out for a drink.

454
00:34:42,110 --> 00:34:47,000
[Cheung Wai Keung: Don't come here anymore.]

455
00:34:52,030 --> 00:34:58,480
[Cheung Wai Keung: Let's all calm down for now.]

456
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:39,190
Loek To.

457
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,190
What's wrong?

458
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:49,630
I know you've been busy and under a lot of pressure lately.

459
00:35:50,030 --> 00:35:52,960
If you need any help, just let me know.

460
00:35:53,480 --> 00:35:54,550
What would I ask you for?

461
00:35:55,840 --> 00:35:57,000
Ask me for help.

462
00:36:01,190 --> 00:36:03,360
You should take over some green industries.

463
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:06,590
Focus on environmental, social, and corporate governance and sustainability.

464
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,030
That kind of thing

465
00:36:09,070 --> 00:36:10,880
can help build the company's brand.

466
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:14,480
Once I build good relationships with the government and environmental groups,

467
00:36:14,630 --> 00:36:16,510
I'm sure we can solve a lot of problems.

468
00:36:18,190 --> 00:36:18,800
Also,

469
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:20,230
my team is very capable.

470
00:36:20,510 --> 00:36:22,710
Seriously, if you really need help,

471
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:23,800
just let me know.

472
00:36:24,030 --> 00:36:26,440
Don't take all the responsibility on yourself.

473
00:36:27,030 --> 00:36:28,630
I can handle the company matters.

474
00:36:31,840 --> 00:36:35,190
Maybe you should stop arguing with Mom.

475
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:41,030
She just wants to save face in front of outsiders.

476
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:42,280
I know how to handle it.

477
00:36:43,670 --> 00:36:44,760
Okay.

478
00:36:54,100 --> 00:36:55,660
[Police]

479
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,630
Team B, Team C, ready?

480
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:08,400
Team B's ready.

481
00:37:09,030 --> 00:37:09,880
Team C's ready.

482
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:18,630
All units, attention. The target is here.

483
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:44,510
Yee Gor, what's wrong?

484
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,150
Got a light?

485
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,590
There are cops.

486
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:01,880
Where did you get the tip?

487
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:03,280
Are you sure it's reliable?

488
00:38:03,590 --> 00:38:04,880
Of course it's reliable.

489
00:38:04,960 --> 00:38:06,630
We can't go through with the deal tonight.

490
00:38:07,030 --> 00:38:08,550
But if we leave without a word,

491
00:38:08,630 --> 00:38:11,440
Lee Fu will get suspicious. That could cause trouble.

492
00:38:11,670 --> 00:38:12,920
Then try telling him

493
00:38:13,510 --> 00:38:15,070
we have someone on the police force.

494
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,000
Guess what he'll think.

495
00:38:23,670 --> 00:38:26,230
We've got a mole among our own people.

496
00:38:27,030 --> 00:38:28,480
See the exit on the right?

497
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Follow me when we leave.

498
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:32,510
But we still can't prove

499
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:33,480
whether they actually are...

500
00:38:33,510 --> 00:38:35,400
Are you being too naive?

501
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,440
Someone just stabbed me in the back.

502
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:41,480
Keep this in mind. Don't sweat the small stuff when you're doing big things.

503
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:45,630
Better they sacrifice themselves than I end up dead, right?

504
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:47,000
Got it, Yee Gor.

505
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:50,630
Oi.

506
00:38:51,030 --> 00:38:53,550
Yee Gor and I are going back to the car for something. Stay here.

507
00:38:53,670 --> 00:38:54,630
Don't wander off.

508
00:38:57,280 --> 00:38:58,800
If I find out who the mole is,

509
00:38:58,840 --> 00:39:00,280
I'll make sure he pays dearly.

510
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:02,630
When this is over,

511
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:04,000
I'll take you all out for roast goose.

512
00:39:04,670 --> 00:39:05,920
Hey, Yee Gor.

513
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:07,000
Seriously?

514
00:39:07,030 --> 00:39:09,230
We're already here. Are you leaving without saying hello?

515
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:10,590
That's not exactly proper, is it?

516
00:39:12,630 --> 00:39:14,000
There are cops everywhere outside.

517
00:39:14,030 --> 00:39:15,190
The deal is off tonight.

518
00:39:16,670 --> 00:39:18,760
Hey, I've got everything ready.

519
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:22,800
All suspects and goods are in place. Move in.

520
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,440
Seal off all their exits immediately.

521
00:39:24,480 --> 00:39:25,400
Don't let a single one get away.

522
00:39:25,510 --> 00:39:27,000
Fu Gor, Yee Gor wasn't lying to you.

523
00:39:27,030 --> 00:39:28,440
We need to leave now.

524
00:39:28,480 --> 00:39:29,400
No.

525
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:30,710
I've got the money ready.

526
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:32,440
I still have customers waiting.

527
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:33,230
The deal has to happen today.

528
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:34,630
Police!

529
00:39:35,230 --> 00:39:36,030
Don't run!

530
00:39:43,030 --> 00:39:43,670
Run!

531
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:47,840
Run!

532
00:39:50,230 --> 00:39:50,840
Don't run!

533
00:39:51,030 --> 00:39:51,630
Don't run!

534
00:40:21,320 --> 00:40:22,070
Come here.

535
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:26,630
Run!

536
00:40:31,670 --> 00:40:33,630
Get down! Hands behind your head! Don't move!

537
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:37,000
Get down!

538
00:40:37,190 --> 00:40:38,000
Cuff him.

539
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:53,710
Go.

540
00:41:08,400 --> 00:41:09,230
Over there.

541
00:41:10,230 --> 00:41:11,070
Go.

542
00:41:19,030 --> 00:41:19,960
Untie this.

543
00:41:35,590 --> 00:41:37,230
Are you kidding? You tied it so tight.

544
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:54,630
Police!

545
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:35,020
[Friday]

546
00:42:47,630 --> 00:42:49,280
What's on the schedule today?

547
00:42:55,670 --> 00:42:56,760
Just say it.

548
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:03,360
Before we start today's schedule,

549
00:43:04,590 --> 00:43:06,440
you might want to take a look at this news report.

550
00:43:08,230 --> 00:43:11,030
Police successfully busted a drug deal last night.

551
00:43:11,230 --> 00:43:13,920
Several suspected core members of a drug-manufacturing ring were arrested.

552
00:43:14,150 --> 00:43:16,230
Among them was a Chinese national surnamed Lee.

553
00:43:16,440 --> 00:43:19,230
Another key member, known as Keung, was shot,

554
00:43:19,280 --> 00:43:20,150
fell into the sea, and remains missing.

555
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:22,550
Police have deployed divers to search for him.

556
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:30,190
Hello?

557
00:43:30,280 --> 00:43:30,840
I'm busy right now.

558
